{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release-critique","packet_sha256":"4318d6c44241dde775fb6b5390e58992c15a4b5d5e1dee757fb7e542f38ba129","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"f6083ade41edf3d3e0acef9fcc57a0b5a6014f8e410e49c3b4c513ca2b5484b4","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"F1","severity":"high","summary":"An unreadable scope observation is treated as absence of a diff, so the no-progress guard can kill a lane precisely when it cannot establish that the lane is unchanged.","evidence":["scripts/task_run/task_run_progress.py: scoped_diff_present catches every observation exception and returns False.","LaneProgressWatch.tick passes that False to no_progress_stop_due, where it is indistinguishable from a successfully observed worktree with no scoped diff.","The scoped_diff_present docstring says an unreadable worktree must not trigger a kill, but the implemented boolean collapses unknown into no-diff.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_implementation_lane.py only asserts that an unobservable tree returns False; it does not exercise an overdue watch with an unobservable tree, which would expose the false stop."],"action":"Represent scoped-diff observation as present/absent/unknown, and permit NO-PROGRESS-STOP only after an affirmative absent observation. Add an overdue-watch test proving observation failure suppresses the kill and remains visible in progress_guard."},{"id":"F2","severity":"medium","summary":"Terminal lane_progress can forget phases that the live watcher already observed, making the durable receipt weaker than the live observability claim.","evidence":["LaneProgressWatch retains observed phases in _last_phases and exposes them through progress_guard.last_phases.","complete_task calls apply_lane_receipt, which reconstructs lane_progress solely from result_delivery.text and _lane_stderr_text instead of merging progress_guard.last_phases.","_lane_stderr_text reads only the final 256 KiB, while the live watcher reads only a 64 KiB tail per poll; early phase markers can therefore disappear from the terminal lane_progress.","test_stderr_scan_is_bounded_to_tail explicitly demonstrates that an early CONTRACT-READ marker is discarded, but no test establishes durable preservation through progress_guard."],"action":"Merge watcher-observed phases into lane_progress, preserving canonical phase order, and record any transcript-observation failure or truncation. Add a completion-level test with an early marker outside the terminal scan window."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The guard begins its budget only after CONTRACT-READ, so a lane that never emits that marker may run until the executor timeout.","bin":"acceptable-by-current-contract","disposition":"The documentation explicitly scopes the early stop to lanes that announced CONTRACT-READ; terminal stall classification still catches a changeless lane without EDITING."},{"concern":"A no-progress stop is classified as failed rather than interrupted.","bin":"not-a-blocker","disposition":"_execution_state deliberately prioritizes progress_stopped, and failed-before-edit remains a known unchanged classification when the checkpoint is skipped. The operator wording could be improved, but this does not mislabel changed work as unchanged."},{"concern":"A zero no-progress budget still records progress_guard.enabled as true.","bin":"follow-up","disposition":"Phase relay remains active, so enabled can describe the watcher even though stopping is disabled; a separate stop_enabled field would make the receipt clearer but is not release-blocking."}],"next_move":"Fix the unknown-versus-no-diff collapse first, then preserve watcher-observed phases in the terminal lane_progress and add the missing failure-path tests before release approval.","non_claims":["No workspace files were read or modified; the review used only the identity-bound inline semantic payload.","No test suite or live executor was run.","The packet is not Goal Run bound.","This review does not approve partial progress or infer behavior from hashes."]}
